# The tutorial window's smaller functions, called the way the game calls them (see tutwin.c): the tests of whether a note is due
# (tut_check and tut_check2: each marks the note shown, so the same bit is due once; the answer is the state's open_result region),
# the window's reset with no note up and with one up, the arrows' window set and the window told it moved, the arrows redrawn, the
# key handler given a key (a letter, which a mode 2 note takes as a key that ends it, and Escape, which also clears the answer), and
# the three callbacks that draw a note's picture (called with a note up).
25 load
26 state tw_fields 0x8cc1e4 0x5c
26 state tw_flags 0x8cc244 8
26 state tw_seen 0x9a64ac 0x14
26 state tw_ans 0x9a64b8 8
26 state tw_draw 0x8c9fd0 4
20 state tw_fields 0x8cc1e4 0x5c
20 state tw_flags 0x8cc244 8
22 snap title            # on the title screen, before a game is loaded: the window as its constructor left it
